window.docContents[29].resolve({"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--External-Cross-References--VIM-4-2CD-___--International-Vocabulary-of-Metrology":{"contents":"Indexed by VIM 4 2CD clause. The 2CD is a restricted committee draft; only clause\nnumbers and terms are recorded.\n\nThe correspondence is mostly with this work's core spine — VIM's quantity,\nratio/interval/ordinal quantity, measurement scale, value of a quantity,\nand the measurement principle/method/procedure chain map directly to PKC\ndeclarations. Three VIM concepts reach into the further layers: quantity\ndimension (1.9) and quantity with the unit one (1.10) are the Dimension\nlayer's dim map and the dimension-one thesis; quantity calculus (1.29) is the\nInteraction algebra; the international system of quantities (1.8) is the\nISO/IEC 80000 catalogue and the coherent derived unit (1.15) the unit each\ncatalogued kind carries.\n\n\n\nMany VIM clauses have no PKC counterpart, for two reasons. Some are metrological-\nprocedure concerns outside this ontology's scope — true value (1.26),\nconventional value (1.27), measurement result (2.10), measured value (2.11),\nmeasurement model/function (2.12–2.13), influence quantity (2.16),\ncorrection (2.17), and the metrology/measurand/primary method terms (2.2,\n2.3, 2.6, 2.8, 2.9). Others are not yet formalized: the base/derived\nquantity and base/derived/off-system unit distinctions (1.6, 1.7,\n1.13, 1.14, 1.18), system of quantities/of units as first-class objects\n(1.5, 1.16, 1.17, 1.19), reference quantity (1.11), the unit/numerical-value\nequation forms (1.31, 1.32), and conversion factor between units (1.22), whose\nround-trip is a planned capstone.\n\n\n","context":"PropertyKindCalculus Blueprint\u0009External Cross-References","header":"24.2. VIM 4 2CD —  International Vocabulary of Metrology","id":"/#PropertyKindCalculus-Blueprint--External-Cross-References--VIM-4-2CD-___--International-Vocabulary-of-Metrology"}});